# Topologies on Algebraic Spaces, Chapter 1: Introduction

The source section is introductory prose.  It announces the study of
topologies on algebraic spaces, cites related references, and records the
qualitative observation that different site presentations can yield the same
sheaf theory and cohomology.  These remarks do not specify a standalone
definition, construction, or theorem interface; the precise site constructions
begin in the next source section, "The general procedure".
